git add -A
echo Committing (no-op if clean)...
git commit -m "Customer template repair: make it automatic, remove the button, kill the timeout. The 'Fix Customer target' button was doing far too much in one request - force-seed the 19-sheet template AND run full AI mapping for every conversion inline - which blew the 60s limit (timeout of 60000ms exceeded). Now it runs automatically at startup via ensure_customer_multisheet(): if no >=5-sheet Customer template exists it force-seeds the bundled HZ_IMP file (bypassing the namesake skip that caused this), then re-points flat-template conversions onto it by changing template_id only and clearing their stale mappings. No inline AI mapping, so it's fast and can't time out; idempotent, so every later boot is a no-op. Removed the button and its handler from the FBDI Templates page. The endpoint stays as a thin manual trigger that just calls the same fast helper. After this deploys the Customer conversion is already on the real 19 sheets - open it, Re-run AI, regenerate."
echo Pushing...
git push origin main
echo.
echo ====== DONE - Press any key to close ======
pause
